From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/35] board: alpine-v2: MUIO pinmux and CCU setup in place of
 the vendor U-Boot

Two things the vendor U-Boot does that al-boot stage3 does not, for when
this U-Boot is stage3's application:
- ALPINE_V2_MUIO_INIT: at board_init, write the <pin function> pairs of
  an "amazon,alpine-v2-muio" DT node into the PBS mux_sel registers
  (4 bits per pin, 8 pins per register, as HAL al_hal_muio_mux.c does on
  Alpine V2), read-modify-write of only those fields;
- ALPINE_V2_CCU_IO_COHERENCY: right before Linux (board_prep_linux, after
  the al_eth handoff), CCI slave interface 4 snoop enable (polling the
  change-pending bit) and speculation control 7, the state the vendor
  bootm leaves for its DT io_coherency. Idempotent.
CMD_ALPINE_V2: "alpine state" prints CCU, NB, MUIO, SGPO and GPIO 16-23
(read-only); "alpine ccu" and "alpine muio" apply the settings by hand.
All three default off; the calls are compiled out then.

Scope: alpine-v2.
---
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig       |  23 ++++
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/Makefile      |   3 +
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.c   |   3 +
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/eth-handoff.c |   3 +
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/soc-init.c    | 167 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/soc-init.h    |   9 ++
 6 files changed, 208 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/amazon/alpine-v2/soc-init.c
 create mode 100644 board/amazon/alpine-v2/soc-init.h

diff --git a/board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig b/board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig
index 710f0f3f..828c2187 100644
--- a/board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig
+++ b/board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig
@@ -32,4 +32,27 @@ config CMD_ALPINE_V2_ETH
 	  "aleth info" shows the board params and MAC of each al_eth
 	  function (read-only); "aleth handoff" writes missing ones now.
 
+config ALPINE_V2_MUIO_INIT
+	bool "Set the MUIO pin functions from the DT at board init"
+	help
+	  Write the <pin function> pairs of the "amazon,alpine-v2-muio" DT
+	  node into the PBS mux_sel registers (only those fields), as the
+	  vendor U-Boot's board-cfg pinctrl_init does. Needed when this
+	  U-Boot runs instead of the vendor one; a no-op after it.
+
+config ALPINE_V2_CCU_IO_COHERENCY
+	bool "Enable CCI snoop and speculation control before Linux"
+	help
+	  Set CCI slave interface 4 snoop enable and speculation control 7
+	  right before Linux, as the vendor bootm does for its DT
+	  io_coherency. Idempotent.
+
+config CMD_ALPINE_V2
+	bool "alpine command"
+	depends on CMDLINE
+	help
+	  "alpine state" prints the CCU, NB, MUIO, SGPO and GPIO registers
+	  that the vendor U-Boot sets up; "alpine ccu" and "alpine muio"
+	  apply the settings above by hand.
+
 endif
